      "writtenOn": "2022-03-29T14:29:57Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "It looks like we call this function shortly before pd_set_power_supply_ready() for Attached.SRC entry at least. The only places I see it called in common code are Attached.SRC entry and run, with one call in the charge manager that I only see old boards using.  In general, I wouldn\u0027t expect it to interrupt Vbus if we run this function to change the current limit for a non-PD port partner so I\u0027m a little surprised it\u0027s interrupting Vbus here. \n\nIs the Vbus interruption due to going from the FRS-triggered Vbus to our regular Vbus sourcing on your chips?  Or did the board\u0027s cached Vbus enable not get updated correctly during the FRS process?",
      "parentUuid": "25112f55_c94c4752",
